@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@

 ### Fixed

+- **`wt config update` no longer overwrites an edit made while its confirmation prompt is open**: the migration was computed before the preview and written after the answer, so a config saved from another terminal during that wait was replaced by the pre-prompt snapshot — silently, with `✓ Updated user config` reported. The command now re-reads each config immediately before writing and fails with the path when the contents have moved on, leaving the newer file in place; re-running previews the current contents.
+
 - **`wt config shell install fish` writes the wrapper where fish reads it under a custom `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`**: the wrapper path was hardcoded to `~/.config/fish/functions/`, while the completion path resolved the XDG config directory — same tool, same command, two answers. With `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME` pointing anywhere but `~/.config`, install reported success for both files, fish autoloaded the completion and never saw the wrapper, so `wt switch` changed no directory and `wt config show` reported the integration as installed. The wrapper, the completion, and the directories `wt config shell uninstall` and `wt config show` scan now all come from one resolution of fish's `$__fish_config_dir`. On Unix an unset or default `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME` is unaffected; on Windows the fish completion moves off `%APPDATA%\fish\completions` onto the same path as the wrapper. The deprecated `conf.d` file install cleans up stays pinned to `~/.config/fish/conf.d`, the only place worktrunk ever wrote it.

 - **`wt remove`, `wt merge`, and `wt step prune` no longer discard untracked files hidden by Git configuration**: `status.showUntrackedFiles = no` made the clean-worktree guard inherit a display preference, so a worktree containing only untracked files appeared clean and could be removed without `--force` — including by `wt step prune`, which removes unattended. Safety checks now always include untracked files and name the path that blocks removal. Auto-staging warnings for `wt merge`, `wt step commit`, and `wt step squash` likewise override the setting and enumerate every file that will be staged.
