`test_docs_commands_are_in_sync` has passed without running since 2025-12-02. It targets `docs/content/commands.md`, which 3f81f285a ("Docs: Split command pages with `--help-page` generation") deleted when the single command page became one page per command — so its first statement is an `exists()` guard that has been false on every run for eight months, and the test returns before it does anything.

```rust
let commands_path = project_root.join("docs/content/commands.md");

if !commands_path.exists() {
    // Skip if docs directory doesn't exist
    return;
}
```

That makes it the shape `running-tend` warns about under **Don't fix tests by adding skip guards** — a green result that asserts nothing. `sync_help_markers` is dead with it: the skipped test is its only caller, so both go.

Nothing else in the file is reachable only from these two. `help_output`, `format_replacement`, `OutputFormat::Unwrapped`, `MARKER_PATTERN`, `trim_lines`, and `MarkerType::Help` all stay live through `sync_readme_markers`, which is the near-identical function that survived the split and still syncs README markers.

No sync coverage is lost. The job this test was written for — keeping rendered `--help` in a docs page current with `after_long_help` — moved to `test_docs_are_in_sync`, whose Step 1 (`sync_command_pages`, `mod.rs` → `docs/content/*.md`) covers the per-command pages that replaced `commands.md`.

## Testing

No regression test: the change deletes test code that cannot execute, so there is nothing to assert about it that the deletion doesn't already settle. Verified instead that the file still compiles warning-free (`cargo test --test integration --no-run`, `cargo clippy --test integration`) and that the remaining 14 `readme_sync` tests pass, `test_docs_are_in_sync` among them.

