body:
Nightly sweep survey finding: the `writing-user-outputs` skill points readers at a `FlagNote` exemplar for symbol color transitions, but names methods that don't exist.

The skill said `FlagNote` handles color transitions "via `after_cyan()` and `after_green()` methods." The actual implementation in `src/output/handlers.rs` has a single method:

```rust
fn after(&self, color: AnsiColor) -> String {
    match &self.symbol {
        Some(s) => match color {
            AnsiColor::Cyan => cformat!("{}<cyan>{}</>", s, self.suffix),
            AnsiColor::Green => cformat!("{}<green>{}</>", s, self.suffix),
            _ => format!("{s}{}", self.suffix),
        },
        None => String::new(),
    }
}
```

`git grep after_cyan\|after_green -- src/` returns nothing — the two named methods have never existed. This corrects the reference to the real `after(color)` method so anyone following the exemplar lands on the actual API.

Doc-only change to a skill file. No test: skill markdown has no runtime surface; correctness is verified by grepping `src/` for the referenced symbols.

