body:
## Summary

Lazy-template expansion was duplicated between `run_one_command` and `run_concurrent_group` in `src/commands/command_executor.rs` — both decoded `context_json`, looked up `lazy_template`, and called `expand_shell_template` with `cmd.label`. Extract a single helper:

```rust
fn resolve_command_str(cmd: &PreparedCommand, repo: &Repository) -> Result<String> {
    match &cmd.lazy_template {
        Some(template) => {
            let context: HashMap<String, String> = serde_json::from_str(&cmd.context_json)
                .context("failed to deserialize context_json")?;
            expand_shell_template(template, &context, repo, &cmd.label)
        }
        None => Ok(cmd.expanded.clone()),
    }
}
```

Returning `String` removes the `lazy_expanded` placeholder binding and avoids a Cow-vs-borrow split. The eager-path clone is cheap.

Lazy-template expansion now exists in exactly one place.

## Test plan

- [x] `cargo run -- hook pre-merge --yes` (3395 tests pass, all lints green)

