## Summary

- Introduces `Cmd` builder in `shell_exec` with same logging/tracing/semaphore benefits as `run()` but cleaner ergonomics
- Adds stdin piping support, eliminating need for manual spawn/write/wait patterns
- Migrates 6 callers including both stdin-requiring cases (`llm.rs`, `select.rs`)

## Before/After

```rust
// Before (verbose, error-prone)
let mut cmd = Command::new("git");
cmd.args(["status"]);
cmd.current_dir(&path);
let output = run(&mut cmd, Some("context"))?;

// After (builder pattern)
let output = Cmd::new("git")
    .args(["status"])
    .current_dir(&path)
    .context("context")
    .run()?;

// Stdin support (was 20+ lines of manual spawn/write/wait)
let output = Cmd::new("git")
    .args(["diff-tree", "--stdin"])
    .stdin(hashes.join("\n"))
    .run()?;
```

